   902|## Step 8 -- the replay harness (D44-D49)
   903|
   904|**Found before building** (offline on the bundle, and read-only live):
   905|- no pair has legs at two timestamps, and the hero's burst starts 09-03 04:54, which is M36 and the reason for D44;
   906|- the full-load fingerprint was taken **before** anything changed (M40's left side). The pre-step state was a full load, so the equivalence check needed one reload, not two;
   907|- COPY cannot filter rows, and `CREATE TABLE ... LIKE` would copy RAW_TRANSACTIONS' constraints and `ingested_at` onto the temporary table.
   908|
   909|**What changed**
   910|- `conf/generation.yml`: the `replay` block (`hold_back_from: null`, `sim_step: 6 hours`, `sleep_seconds: 5`, `batch_legs: 500`, `injections: {structuring_burst: structuring}`). `conf/profiles/dev.yml`: `hold_back_from: 2022-09-03 00:00:00` (D44). `generate`'s output does not depend on this block: the manifest records no config.
   911|- `config.py`:
   912|  - `duration_seconds()` is the one parser of the `<n> hour(s)` grammar, shared with `TARGET_LAG`;
   913|  - a typed `ReplaySpec`, exposed as `Settings.replay`, and checked at load when present. It refuses a bad duration, `batch_legs < 1`, a negative sleep, a zoned timestamp, and an injection naming an unknown cohort. A YAML date means that day's midnight.
   914|- `pipeline/load.py` (D48):
   915|  - `Loader(hold_back=...)` deletes the copied source legs at or after the cut and promotes only the pending legs before it, all in the load transaction;
   916|  - two new checks, "source legs held back for replay" and "injected legs promoted" net of the held-back ones;
   917|  - `promotion_sql` takes filters and is anti-joined on `txn_id`;
   918|  - `Loader.promote(filters)` is the one promotion path; `PendingFilter` / `window_filters` are its predicates;
   919|  - `upload_artifact` PUTs one bundle file to its content-addressed folder;
   920|  - `raw_fingerprint` is the `HASH_AGG` over every column but `ingested_at`, with the columns from INFORMATION_SCHEMA;
   921|  - the loader's helpers are public (`sql`, `scalar`, `table`), because replay uses them.
   922|- New `pipeline/replay.py`:
   923|  - `held_back_legs` / `plan_ticks`: the offline plan (D45);
   924|  - `Replayer.run`:
   925|    1. check the bundle's hashes;
   926|    2. plan;
   927|    3. PUT the bundle's RAW_TRANSACTIONS (skipped when it is already staged);
   928|    4. a zero-row CTAS into a session TEMPORARY table, then the loader's COPY into it, row count checked;
   929|    5. preflight: refuse a leg this bundle did not write, and a load that held back more;
   930|    6. skip the ticks already complete;
   931|    7. per tick, one transaction: `INSERT ... SELECT` of the window's source legs, anti-joined, whose count must equal the plan, then `promote` of the window's pending legs;
   932|    8. three post-replay checks: every planned leg arrived, 0 pending unresolved, no txn_id twice.
   933|
   934|    It never refreshes and never routes.
   935|  - `inject`: one host's pending cohort legs, selected by pair through RAW_ACCOUNTS, in one transaction (D47);
   936|  - `_roll_back` (D49).
   937|- `cli.py`:
   938|  - `load --hold-back/--no-hold-back` (default on); `load` prints the cut;
   939|  - `replay` replaces the stub: it streams with a line per tick, and `--inject NAME [--party P]` releases and exits;
   940|  - before connecting, `replay` refuses `--party` without `--inject` (exit 2) and a null hold-back (exit 2).
